On Midgard the DRAW descriptor aliases "Thread Storage" and "FBD" onto the
same bits (start 28:0 in genxml/v5.xml), so the value stored in the batch's
thread storage slot must carry the FRAMEBUFFER_POINTER tag, not a bare
descriptor address.

The Gallium v5 path does this by packing FRAMEBUFFER_POINTER with
render_target_count and storing the tagged result. The forward port stored the
raw address instead, so the tiler job read an untagged framebuffer pointer.
On the T830 that surfaced as a job fault on the tiler slot with
DATA_INVALID_FAULT, fault pointer equal to the framebuffer descriptor, and the
v5 decoder warning "Unexpected framebuffer pointer settings". The fragment job
then faulted on the polygon list body the tiler had never populated.

With the tag applied, the same image renders a verified triangle on the T830:
"panvk: T830 static triangle pixels verified checksum=355e1a23" and
"GPU: Vulkan status=0 frames=1 checksum=355e1a23 display_restored=1", with no
js fault, DATA_INVALID or MMU fault anywhere in the boot.

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/jm/panvk_vX_cmd_buffer.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/jm/panvk_vX_cmd_buffer.c
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/jm/panvk_vX_cmd_buffer.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/jm/panvk_vX_cmd_buffer.c
@@ -224,7 +224,20 @@ panvk_per_arch(cmd_alloc_tls_desc)(struct panvk_cmd_buffer *cmdbuf, bool gfx)
       VkResult result = panvk_per_arch(cmd_alloc_fb_desc)(cmdbuf);
       if (result != VK_SUCCESS)
          return result;
-      batch->tls = batch->fb.desc;
+      /* On Midgard the thread storage pointer is the framebuffer descriptor
+       * itself, tagged the same way the tiler job's FBD field is: the DRAW
+       * struct aliases "Thread Storage" and "FBD" onto bits 28:0, so the value
+       * handed to both must carry the FRAMEBUFFER_POINTER tag. Storing the raw
+       * descriptor address here made the tiler read an untagged pointer and
+       * fault with DATA_INVALID. Mirror what the Gallium v5 path does.
+       */
+      struct mali_framebuffer_pointer_packed tag;
+      pan_pack(tag.opaque, FRAMEBUFFER_POINTER, cfg) {
+         cfg.zs_crc_extension_present = false;
+         cfg.render_target_count = 1;
+      }
+      batch->tls.cpu = batch->fb.desc.cpu;
+      batch->tls.gpu = batch->fb.desc.gpu | tag.opaque[0];
       return VK_SUCCESS;
    }
 #endif
